# Review routing. Every entry must be a GitHub username (or org team) with at least
# write access to this repository — GitHub silently ignores invalid owners, so a typo
# here means no review is ever requested. Validate after editing:
#
#   gh api repos/xsolla/xsolla-ai-kit/codeowners/errors
#
# NOTE: these are GitHub handles, not Xsolla LDAP names. The `metadata.owner` field in
# each SKILL.md uses an internal LDAP-style id instead — but not one consistent format
# (existing skills mix `firstname.lastname`, `firstname_lastname`, and `f-lastname`).
# The two fields intentionally differ; don't "fix" an owner into a format the repo
# doesn't actually use. See CONTRIBUTING-skills.md and VALID_OWNERS in
# .github/scripts/validate_skills.py.

# Who reviews what
#
# Each team reviews its own skills. A change to a skill needs that team's approval,
# not a central reviewer. The AI Kit maintainers own the platform: CI, the validator,
# the generated files, AGENTS.md and the contributor guides.
#
# Adding a new skill: add its CODEOWNERS line for your team in the same PR. The
# maintainers then review only that line and the platform files you touched.
#
# GitHub uses the LAST matching line, so domain lines below override the default.

